# sync_timedb startup tar seal contract

`sync_timedb` runs a **startup-only** background pass that seals and drops uncompressed daily `.tar` files when **no closed raw stats remain on the filesystem** for that calendar day. This reclaims disk under ingest backlog without modifying janitor **`DAY_CLOSE`** workflow.

## Canonical module

| Concern | Location |
|---|---|
| Discover, eligibility, slice loop, manifest | `hpcperfstats/dbload/sync_timedb_startup_tar_seal.py` → `StartupTarSealPreflight` |
| Supervisor wiring | `run_sync_timedb_supervisor_loop` in `sync_timedb.py` |
| Seal primitive (reuse only) | `atomic_seal_tar_to_zst` in `sync_timedb_archive_helpers.py` |

## Startup behavior (default `sync_startup_tar_seal_preflight=yes`)

Immediately after **`StartupRawRemovalPreflight.start_async_verify()`** and **`StartupDayClosePreflight.start_async_discover_and_close()`**, the supervisor starts **`StartupTarSealPreflight.start_async_seal()`** on thread `sync_timedb.py [thread:startup-tar-seal-preflight]`. Ingest begins **without waiting** on tar seal completion (**no ingest gate**).

| Step | Behavior |
|---|---|
| **Discover** | `iter_daily_tar_paths`; oldest calendar day first |
| **Eligibility** | `.tar` on disk; `is_daily_tar_sealed_dirty`; closed raw grouped by daily tar via **filesystem scan only** (filename epoch / mtime — no parallel head-metadata read); `daily_tar_seal_calendar_eligible` |
| **Skip** | Active append for that daily tar only; days with active/submitted **`AsyncDayCloseCoordinator`** work (`has_async_day_close_for_tar`); not full janitor disqualification |
| **Action** | `atomic_seal_tar_to_zst` + `effective_keep_uncompressed_tar`; `invalidate_daily_archive_members_cache` on success |
| **Resume** | Manifest `{archive_data_dir}/.sync_timedb_startup_tar_seal.json`; **`phase=done` means tar-seal scope is exhausted** (no actionable pending tars), **not** “no dirty `.tar` on disk”. Days blocked by closed raw / async day-close are recorded as manifest skips; janitor **`DAY_CLOSE`** clears raw later. Full rediscover when interval elapsed and live/coordinator remaining signature changes; **`interval <= 0`** disables periodic rediscover after initial discover (tests only — no **0.25s** poll loop after `phase=done`). |
| **Completion log** | Use `blocked_skips`, `blocked_remaining_raw`, `blocked_async_day_close` — not `blocked_by_day_close` for all skip reasons. |
| **Canonical scan** | Derive `remaining_by_tar` from **`StartupArchiveScanCoordinator`** snapshot when available (`sync-timedb-canonical-startup-archive-scan.mdc`); one full collect per pass, not a **0.25s** rescan loop. |

INI tunables ( `[PIPELINE]` ): `sync_startup_tar_seal_budget_seconds` (default **300**), `sync_startup_tar_seal_days_per_slice` (default **1**), `sync_startup_tar_seal_rediscover_interval_seconds` (default **600**), `sync_startup_snapshot_wait_seconds` (default **300**, min **120**).

## Forbidden patterns

- Routing startup tar reclaim through **`DAY_CLOSE`** / `_close_one_day`
- Blocking supervisor ingest on tar seal completion
- Editing `build_seal_disqualified_daily_tars` for this feature
- Raw delete in this pass (raw absence is eligibility precondition; use startup raw removal or janitor)

